exit 0
--- stdout
Docs · 85 asks                                                         20 topics

agents  add a sub-agent for every project or for one, choose the model it
  runs, and remove it
  see which sub-agents exist and their models
    → tofu agents
  add a sub-agent to this project
    → tofu agents add <name> --description "<what it does>" --model <source/model>
  add a sub-agent to every project
    → tofu agents add --global <name> --description "<what it does>" --model <source/model>
  run a sub-agent on another model
    → tofu agents set <name> <source/model>
  remove a sub-agent I added
    → tofu agents remove <name>
  set up three sub-agents at once, each on its own model
    → tofu agents add <name> --description "<what it does>" --model <source/model>, once per sub-agent

browser  how tofu reads and drives your Chrome tabs, the tofu tab group, the
  badge, and what tofu never does there
  connect tofu to Chrome
    → tofu browser install
  let the model read the Chrome tabs tofu can reach
    → tofu settings set browser read
  let the model click and type in the tabs tofu can reach
    → tofu settings set browser drive
  take the browser tools away from the model
    → tofu settings set browser off
  let jev pick each browser step toward a whole goal instead of the model
    → tofu settings set browserDriver goal
  allow fewer actions in one browser task
    → tofu settings set browserSteps 10

commands  every slash command the app's composer takes, how /compact shrinks
  the history the next turn carries, and how /undo puts files back
  free room in the context before the next turn
    → /compact in the app, between turns
  undo what the last turn changed
    → tofu undo, or /undo in the app

cron  jobs that post a prompt into the session on a timer or after each turn,
  how to change one, and the history of every change
  repeat a prompt every few minutes
    → /loop 10m check the build
  keep working until a test passes
    → /goal make the test pass --until "go test ./..."
  change when a scheduled job fires
    → /cron edit c1 --schedule "every 30m" --reason "the build is stable"
  stop a scheduled job
    → /cron delete c1

doctor  what tofu doctor checks, what each line it prints means, and what to
  do about it
  find out why tofu will not start
    → tofu doctor
  check that tofu can run here
    → tofu doctor
  stop rewriting shell commands through rtk
    → write use off in .tofu/tools/shell/proxy.yaml
  check the library files and these pages
    → tofu library

drive  what tofu drive does, the steps a script takes, and what the requests
  step prints

files  every path tofu uses in your home and in a project, and which one wins
  where does tofu keep its files
    → tofu docs files

gate  what jev judges before a tool call runs, when tofu asks you first, and
  where the OpenRouter key lives
  store the openrouter key the gate needs
    → tofu login classifier openrouter
  why was a tool call refused or asked about
    → tofu why --last
  tell tofu a verdict was wrong
    → tofu label --last allow
  judge a command without running it
    → tofu check "<command>"
  see how other thresholds would have decided
    → tofu replay --point tool_gate --set risk_ask_at=1.5
  work one task with the gate off
    → tofu run --dir . --no-gate "<task>"

hooks  the Claude Code and codex hooks tofu runs around a tool call, a prompt
  and a turn's end, and how a project's hooks are trusted
  see the Claude Code and codex hooks tofu runs here
    → tofu hooks
  trust this project's hooks
    → tofu hooks trust
  turn every hook off in this project
    → write "disableAllHooks" true in .claude/settings.local.json

instructions  which AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md files tofu sends with every task,
  in what order, and how to change that
  give tofu house rules for every project
    → write them in ~/.tofu/AGENTS.md
  see which instruction files tofu sends
    → tofu run --dir . --show-prompt "anything"
  work one task without my instruction files
    → tofu run --dir . --no-instructions "<task>"

keys  the keys the app answers to, which ones you can rebind, and finding a
  prompt you sent before with ctrl+p
  find a prompt I sent in another session
    → ctrl+p in the app, type part of it, then enter

models  sign in to a subscription, name a model as source/model, choose the
  model a task runs, and set the tiers
  sign in with a subscription
    → tofu login llm claude-sub
  see which models I can use
    → tofu models
  use a model my subscription just started serving
    → tofu models reload
  run the next task on another model
    → /models in the app, then pick a model
  always run the orchestrator on one model
    → write model: <source/model> in ~/.tofu/roles/orchestrator.yaml
  stop tofu from using a model
    → write use: excluded and a reason in ~/.tofu/models/<provider>/<model>.yaml
  how much subscription quota is left
    → tofu usage

rules  add your own rules for every project or for one, switch a rule off, and
  see which rules run
  add a rule for every project
    → tofu rules add --global <id> "<text>"
  add a rule to this project only
    → tofu rules add <id> "<text>"
  switch off a rule tofu ships
    → tofu rules off <id> --reason "<why>"
  change what a rule tofu ships says, for this project
    → tofu rules add <id> "<text>" --reason "<why>"
  see which rules I overrode and why
    → tofu rules overrides
  bring back a rule I switched off or overrode
    → tofu rules restore <id>
  remove a rule I added
    → tofu rules remove <id>
  see which rules run and where each one comes from
    → tofu rules list

serve  tofu serve --stdio speaks tofu.host/1, JSON-RPC over standard input and
  output, for the desk app or any script
  drive tofu from another program over standard input and output
    → tofu serve --stdio

sessions  continue where you left off, find an old session, and where sessions
  and running shells are kept
  move old sessions out of the project
    → tofu migrate
  continue where I left off
    → tofu --continue
  open an older session
    → tofu session resume <name|id>
  give a session a name
    → tofu session rename <name|id> "<new name>"
  see how full the context window got
    → tofu context

settings  every setting, its default, what it takes, and how to change it
  run commands without asking me first
    → tofu settings set gatePrompt run
  ask me before a gated command runs
    → tofu settings set gatePrompt ask
  change the colours
    → tofu settings set theme Nord
  stop the animations
    → tofu settings set animations off
  show every tool call in the chat
    → tofu settings set chatShowsTools true
  hide the model's thinking
    → tofu settings set showThinking false
  let tofu edit a file it has not read
    → tofu settings set readBeforeEdit false
  use another shell, or wsl
    → tofu settings set shell wsl
  keep shells running after tofu exits
    → tofu settings set persistentRegistry true
  stop sub-agents from being spawned
    → tofu settings set turnMaySpawn false
  allow more sub-agents in one task
    → tofu settings set subAgentsPerTurn 20
  pick the model a sub-agent tier runs
    → tofu settings set modelTier.smart claude-sub/claude-sonnet-5
  read CLAUDE.md, not AGENTS.md, where a folder has both
    → tofu settings set instructionSources claude-first
  send more of my instruction files each turn
    → tofu settings set projectInstructionsCap 65536
  read sub-agents only from .tofu
    → tofu settings set agentSources tofu
  turn skills off
    → tofu settings set skills off
  never attach pasted images
    → tofu settings set images off
  change a setting for one project only
    → tofu settings set --scope project <key> <value>
  see every setting and where it came from
    → tofu settings

shells  why a long build moves to a background shell, how the model reads it
  back, and what its row shows
  stop a server an agent left running
    → tofu shells stop <name>
  read the output of a running shell
    → tofu shells log <name>
  why a long build moved to a background shell
    → tofu docs shells

skills  where tofu finds skills, how to add one for every project or for one,
  and how to turn skills off
  add a skill for every project
    → write ~/.tofu/skills/<name>/SKILL.md with a name and a description
  add a skill to this project only
    → write .tofu/skills/<name>/SKILL.md with a name and a description
  see which skills the model is offered
    → tofu run --dir . --show-prompt "anything"

start  what tofu is, the first commands to type, and where to read more
  see what changed in this version
    → tofu changelog

update  how tofu update finds the latest release, checks it and replaces the
  tofu you run
  update tofu to the latest release
    → tofu update
  is there a newer tofu
    → tofu update --check

  → tofu docs <topic>
  → tofu docs "a few words"
